{
  // DOD-M12B-TESTS-NOT-TYPECHECKED-1 — a FOOTHOLD, deliberately not the whole thing.
  //
  // Every package excludes `src/__tests__` from `tsc --build`, so a test asserting on a field that
  // does not exist, or calling a method that was removed, is invisible to the gate — it fails only
  // if vitest happens to execute that line. That is the hollow-test shape every review in this
  // milestone has hunted, institutionalised. It already let a defect ship: `msg-018` called
  // `ensureStandingReceiverForAgent` with two arguments against a one-parameter signature and
  // `pnpm run typecheck` reported exit 0.
  //
  // Switching it on repo-wide surfaces **339** errors in the daemon's existing tests alone — mostly
  // deliberate partial fakes that need `as unknown as` casts, which is a real cleanup and not this
  // unit. So this covers the files added by the interrupted-session work plus the shared helpers,
  // which is where the defect shipped and where a regression would land next. Widening it is
  // `DOD-M12B-TESTS-NOT-TYPECHECKED-1`; add files here as they are cleaned.
  //
  // `files` rather than `include`, because `exclude` in the base config filters `include` and would
  // drop every one of these.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "src"
  ],
  "files": [
    // `DOD-M15-SEALWIRE-1` B2b-1 pass-2 F3. Both are NEW and clean, which is this list's stated
    // admission criterion — and both contained a real type error the gate could not see: they
    // passed `undefined` for `leafKind`, which is now `number`, and it was silently rebuilt one hop
    // below by `submitMessageHash`'s own default. A test file outside this allowlist is a file where
    // "the mutants are typecheck failures now" is not true.
    // Added on creation, per the trap in RESUME STATE: a test file outside this list is one where
    // "the mutants are typecheck failures now" is not true.
    "src/__tests__/dod-m15-salt-adoption-rule.test.ts",
